// Fixture: suspending `-> { health: int }` (anon-shape return) must be rejected with a
// readable diagnostic — not a raw internal name like `__anon__health__int`.
//
// WHY: WideValueSuspendingReturn guard (Round-22 FIX a). The diagnostic used to call
// `type_name` on the raw internal shape name, printing "__anon__health__int" instead of
// "{ health: int }". This leaked compiler-internal naming into user-facing output (Golden
// Rule 11 violation). The fix routes all Shape name rendering through `type_name()`, which
// formats anon shapes as `{ field: type }` pairs. This fixture verifies the readable form
// appears in stderr.
//
// Expected: exit code 1, diagnostic says "cannot yet return" and mentions "{ health: int }".
// Expected: no stdout (compile error, no binary produced).
function sleepingAnon() -> { health: int } {
  wait sleep(5)
  return { health: 42 }
}

function entrypoint() -> nothing {
  const r = sleepingAnon()
  print(r.health.toString())
}
